# kiss_ai projects ownership

## `_kiss_ai/` — shared hub and framework code

- `_kiss_ai/` contains the shared local hub/framework code, including `framework/**` and `web/**`.
- `_kiss_ai/framework/` is the canonical framework for agentic builds.
- `_kiss_ai/web/` is the shared web app for managed projects.
- Edit `_kiss_ai/**` when the user asks to change hub/framework behavior or tooling.
- Do not treat `_kiss_ai/` itself as a managed research project.
- Do not recreate copied `framework/` folders inside managed project roots.

## Managed research project roots

- For normal research work, prefer root `human_*.md` requirement files.
- Use `inputs_human/` for notes, sources, and uploads.
- Run build commands from the selected project root, but follow the central command docs under `_kiss_ai/framework/commands/`.
- Keep Git status, diffs, annotation detection, and snapshot commits scoped to the selected project root.

## AI-managed areas

- In managed project roots, treat `inputs_ai/**` and `outputs_ai/**` as AI-managed output areas.
- Preserve human annotations there; do not silently overwrite annotated content.
